ed-solution "The vertex of a right-opening parabola is the left-most point of the parabola.\n\n![](images/cd/cd9376f67191ac00f58fa74a066d69008b2d43e6743af62ee6577911374ff5eb.png)\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(6,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67455965-c9d3-5ae8-8b56-2a58af95df0a" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Vertex of a Vertical Parabola Given Its Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11ba3512-eaa8-5321-aa96-abe2a946d071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555034} {:answer/id #uuid "81efdfb9-02a6-5ea4-a9eb-5456a31d6ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555299} {:answer/id #uuid "8406d667-63ff-58a4-a718-2dd90e66256a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555304} {:answer/id #uuid "95dd750a-51eb-54bf-b675-b53b71df0478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555359} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a81445-6e86-5d1f-baeb-5cb9f1dca3d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5a81445-6e86-5d1f-baeb-5cb9f1dca3d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555508} :answer-field/id #uuid "d580fbee-d419-5754-8c6e-c8cdde3856be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b28f59d7-76e7-504d-aaab-0c27b75b3222" :question/math-academy-id "q-115904" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $(x-4)^{2}=-24(y+5)?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2} & =4(-6)(y+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-6.$\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=4$ and $k=-5.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(4,-5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e302810-8b14-5c8c-8bbb-245386a66b7c" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Vertex of a Horizontal Parabola Given Its Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e170e66-986b-586b-aa37-931b2ef7939d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555252} {:answer/id #uuid "87865efc-4d97-556d-b25c-84be8a361ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555314} {:answer/id #uuid "8a02ee2b-c276-5b3b-b415-d7b395c5780c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555321} {:answer/id #uuid "90e56bb0-d61e-5cde-bde8-277de6795d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555340} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c30631-442c-5970-930d-6fbc7ef97378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(16,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87865efc-4d97-556d-b25c-84be8a361ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555314} :answer-field/id #uuid "38d93762-7c0b-561a-b5d6-707d86a75a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b2b25e3-0202-54b4-aedb-ceb8981dd37f" :question/math-academy-id "q-115907" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${y}^{2}=16x?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4(4)x.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=4.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67455965-c9d3-5ae8-8b56-2a58af95df0a" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Vertex of a Vertical Parabola Given Its Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b92942c-8aba-5aa1-868e-af6ff0b747b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555050} {:answer/id #uuid "6332f8e1-70e3-52dc-ba10-2ad158c200d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555219} {:answer/id #uuid "6de35bfe-a94a-5f6f-a2a7-be882652597a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555251} {:answer/id #uuid "98125233-946f-554a-8efb-6031235b27b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555364} {:answer/id #uuid "f833dfc3-dd27-5cc6-a187-eb5f1348d40e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b92942c-8aba-5aa1-868e-af6ff0b747b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555050} :answer-field/id #uuid "eada811c-d053-5120-a961-fe8ffd045312" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9b1a0e36-dce4-509e-90b0-4f68fe84ad7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-84968" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $(x+5)^{2}=-3(y-6)?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{3}{4})(y-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=-5$ and $k=6.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(-5,6).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e302810-8b14-5c8c-8bbb-245386a66b7c" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Vertex of a Horizontal Parabola Given Its Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e4a15a-eda1-52a1-8baa-9cdce6bed32e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-\\